      "answer": "$\\frac{343\\pi}{6}$",
      "official_mark_scheme_text": "Intersections: $\\frac12x+\\frac4x=4.5\\Rightarrow x^2-9x+8=0$ — M1; $x=1,8$ — A1 SOI. Cylinder volume $\\pi(4.5)^2(8-1)=\\frac{567\\pi}{4}$ — A1FT using their positive limits. Curve volume: $\\pi\\int_1^8(\\frac12x+\\frac4x)^2dx$ — *M1. Expand/integrate to $\\pi\\int(\\frac14x^2+4+16x^{-2})dx=\\pi(\\frac1{12}x^3+4x-\\frac{16}{x})$ — A1 for two correct terms and A1 for all three; may be unsimplified and include $+C$. Substitute their positive limits clearly — DM1; at least one correct power required, or with correct limits the minimum accepted expression is $\\frac{218}{3}+\\frac{143}{12}$ up to sign. Volume $=\\frac{343\\pi}{6}$ — A1; condone negative changed positive, A0 without $\\pi$; SC B1 following DM0, A0 for 179.594… . Alternative washer method: $\\pi\\int_1^8[(4.5)^2-(\\frac12x+\\frac4x)^2]dx$ — *M1; condone the reversed difference for this method. Antiderivative $\\pi(4.5^2x-\\frac1{12}x^3-4x+\\frac{16}{x})$ — A1 for each of the three curve elements, may be unsimplified and include $+C$; terms derived from the reversed difference score A0A0A0 XP. Substitute their positive limits — DM1; with correct limits the minimum accepted expression is $\\frac{268}{3}-\\frac{193}{6}$ up to sign. Volume $=\\frac{343\\pi}{6}$ — A1 with the same sign, $\\pi$, SC and decimal conditions. Total 8.",
